{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792851803,"nonce":"cVIoCrIGIXOLr9+sW3HDZhj+tj8=","title":"TypeScript: string and number literal types","message":"Literal type annotations were 'this type representation' gaps. The module's string and number literal types become two literal enums, so a literal type is a member type and a literal union a member union, sharing the enum checks: a matching literal (or a const holding one) is assignable, a widened string or number is TypeScript's 2322, comparisons without overlap are 2367, equality narrows, and a switch whose literal cases cover the union is exhaustive. Boolean literal types, literal-typed fields and arrays, literal unions mixed with other types and exported declarations using enum or literal member types stay Unsupported; the export guard now also covers enum member types.","files":null}]}